#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184051 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "8f36c3e6-0c27-5b89-9f8d-5ec6b2f9e614" :question/math-academy-id "e-9821" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}) \\: \\textrm{mi}$ with a constant velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{mi/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $\\mathbf{u},$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 3\\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 2 \\: \\textrm{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(3j-i)+(i-j)(2) \\\\  & =(-i+3j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(i+j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184052 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/id #uuid "2d8b9078-4e19-5f6d-b4cb-95f0c7ee07d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-9822" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(4\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j})\\,\\textrm{cm}$ with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/min}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(\\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $4$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 4\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} + 3\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 4 \\, \\textrm{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(4i-j)+(i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+3j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i-j)+(4i+4j)+8(i+3j) \\\\  & =(8i+3j)+(8i+24j) \\\\  & =(16i+27j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184053 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/id #uuid "ca75ba70-5bef-5c21-ba01-1ad50faa0da2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9824" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{cm/s}^2$ and an initial velocity of $(-\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}) \\: \\textrm{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $\\mathbf{a},$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\mathbf{r}_0 + \\mathbf{u} t + \\dfrac12 \\mathbf{a} t^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}_0$ is the initial position of the particle and $\\mathbf{u}$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}_0 = 0\\mathbf i +0 \\mathbf j , \\qquad \\mathbf u = -\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = \\mathbf{i} +\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t = 6 \\, \\textrm{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(-i-2j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+18(i+j) \\\\  & =(-6i-12j)+(18i+18j) \\\\  & =(12i+6j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c43185c6-59e3-564d-9f23-31497d128211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306638} {:answer/id #uuid "85e7156b-ef57-5373-8292-d67345db8b26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i+4j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306639} {:answer/id #uuid "955d1aa7-330e-5cde-9f50-2e874b909d77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i-8j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306640} {:answer/id #uuid "d8829320-7fbc-56bc-8a7e-720c42582b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306641} {:answer/id #uuid "a9329fae-ed7b-5911-8b55-ddf2e78423c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2j\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8829320-7fbc-56bc-8a7e-720c42582b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306641} :answer-field/id #uuid "a25069e5-e29e-5424-9441-b52946e5ed61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "afe1f0be-e3c3-5ca8-ae7c-e8a7cf49172c" :question/math-academy-id "q-136375" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(i-4j)\\,\\text{km}$ with a constant velocity of $i\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ hours." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=i-4j,\\,u=i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(i-4j)+i(2) \\\\  & =(i-4j)+2i \\\\  & =(3i-4j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2c7c0f5-bbee-5b10-9beb-c053dc6b02b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3j\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306645} {:answer/id #uuid "7707adf1-96b2-52ca-9ee1-3e48596b651c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+8j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306646} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d24a6f-4136-5ddd-ab66-2521a932d41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306647} {:answer/id #uuid "ab833d1f-0614-5eca-b331-f371ab8009a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3i\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306648} {:answer/id #uuid "375697bb-e1cd-58a8-bdd6-128612fe2c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1d24a6f-4136-5ddd-ab66-2521a932d41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306647} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7832a4-4762-5c0f-a672-3556e5a82f6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2e0ff07-fc5d-5fc3-af79-a12180dc0106" :question/math-academy-id "q-136379" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of  $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(2i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i+15j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4875e8-5487-5ab7-96a7-0d77e7d194a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4i-7j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306651} {:answer/id #uuid "e4571d5a-445a-5b9e-b93d-210bf8fe49fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16i+49j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306652} {:answer/id #uuid "c826faa3-9ccf-5b37-91b0-f036170396e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25i+36j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306653} {:answer/id #uuid "5678055e-a5fe-5883-9892-528f0e2caaf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3i-8j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306654} {:answer/id #uuid "5f974428-619f-5125-ba74-0bae2af9a1a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f974428-619f-5125-ba74-0bae2af9a1a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306655} :answer-field/id #uuid "27d20681-f8f5-5211-8cd3-9f1bfb441efa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b69163c-7d60-5882-a4d4-0cf0337f664b" :question/math-academy-id "q-136413" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(-i+j)\\,\\text{mm}$ with an acceleration of $(2i-6j)\\,{\\text{mm/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{mm/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $5$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-i+j,\\,u=-3i+2j,\\,a=2i-6j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-i+j)+(-3i+2j)(5)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i-6j)(5)^{2} \\\\  & =(-i+j)+(-15i+10j)+25(i-3j) \\\\  & =(-16i+11j)+(25i-75j) \\\\  & =(9i-64j)\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df51e8c-cc9e-545d-aefe-09673c2327e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i-j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306658} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb390af-5318-576f-9193-fa7560a8cfdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306659} {:answer/id #uuid "41badbec-bece-52e6-ac87-c8c50be5286c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7i-14j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306660} {:answer/id #uuid "893062d6-429d-52ce-b27b-25b17d0ddfd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7j\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306661} {:answer/id #uuid "252b5abf-0395-5a09-9f93-624057fde26c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15i+5j)\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb390af-5318-576f-9193-fa7560a8cfdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306659} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff4f095b-07d9-5f63-aa1b-a9904baa0645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4eb6abc7-15cc-58dd-b3c7-5a5145bf8306" :question/math-academy-id "q-136416" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $-2j\\,\\text{ft}$ with an acceleration of $4i\\,{\\text{ft/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{ft/min}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $2$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-2j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=4i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=2\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-2j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(4i)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-2j+(6i+2j)+2(4i) \\\\  & =6i+8i \\\\  & =14i\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04def214-8643-58a5-b6a7-d8c74c77fc30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306665} {:answer/id #uuid "97650060-4361-571a-8691-dc19e5485507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306666} {:answer/id #uuid "bb76d237-7722-51d3-8ab7-520d34fdb02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306667} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4296c4-14e9-5435-a6b2-73dae5db1228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306668} {:answer/id #uuid "56668588-fe5e-52ba-967f-3b85139a6dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56668588-fe5e-52ba-967f-3b85139a6dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306669} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3968006-1b2a-5f80-b663-94b9abfa4d42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "777df686-1714-5c34-b776-17560f153c50" :question/math-academy-id "q-136436" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(4) \\\\  & =(12i+4j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12i+4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{160} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbd4a581-cdb6-5523-993c-29d20e36455a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306672} {:answer/id #uuid "b919c316-9c63-5924-ba69-ec6a8cf477b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306673} {:answer/id #uuid "09c64337-3ee6-55ed-8558-389a57fc3f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306674} {:answer/id #uuid "77a8c9d6-3f34-5935-ba08-3074065ddf69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306675} {:answer/id #uuid "07dc82b3-c15c-5cc5-89aa-484f22b160d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbd4a581-cdb6-5523-993c-29d20e36455a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306672} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb59414-3bd0-5713-8f4b-deb27157d182" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "889ae6c0-54a0-5d30-bfc5-d1d48e052f8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-136437" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i-4j)\\,\\text{m},$ with an acceleration of $(-i+j)\\,{\\text{m/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/min}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-4j,\\,u=3i-j,\\,a=-i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=6\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-4j)+(3i-j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-4j)+(18i-6j)+18(-i+j) \\\\  & =(20i-10j)+(-18i+18j) \\\\  & =(2i+8j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35d68f32-6855-5dd5-8169-f0ef2b45642d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306679}] :an