ition Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60d624ca-9a4e-50d7-b652-9d26f9feff91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306684} {:answer/id #uuid "d6db4ceb-dd07-59fa-851a-6c4ba22c6c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6db4ceb-dd07-59fa-851a-6c4ba22c6c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306685} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6f8ce6c-49fb-5518-a6dd-9033e4001547" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0de7ae8-02db-52c7-84c5-aaa713340284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0de7ae8-02db-52c7-84c5-aaa713340284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306687} :answer-field/id #uuid "00fb7d77-7f97-5598-82cb-39a142a125fb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9ba8e59-9cf8-5def-afd8-4dae30f24f5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280491" :question/problem "A bird glides with a constant velocity of $(-2i-1j)\\,\\text{yd/s}.$ If it starts at the position ${r}_{0}=(6i+4j)\\,\\text{yd},$ find its position vector $r$ after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{yd}$" :question/worked-solution "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=6i+4j,\\,u=-2i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the bird after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(6i+4j)+(-2i-1j)(3) \\\\  & =6i+4j-6i-3j \\\\  & =(\\,0\\,i+1\\,j)\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54dcd1d-56f5-527d-9f24-ff4b7d221d06" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbdd8c89-f4ec-5793-915e-ef0c97a79e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbdd8c89-f4ec-5793-915e-ef0c97a79e60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306690} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec0b6b9-1323-59c8-8164-ae7ffa8d38bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db0ce9c-6788-57b1-994c-2261c75d22d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0db0ce9c-6788-57b1-994c-2261c75d22d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306692} :answer-field/id #uuid "5790369e-5d68-5053-b0c1-c5d14c5f0365" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7079cd9b-c2d6-5c5c-a2d9-8bcbd89f6dad" :question/math-academy-id "q-280492" :question/problem "An autonomous submarine travels with a constant velocity of $(3i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ If its initial position is ${r}_{0}=(-3i+0j)\\,\\text{km},$ find the position vector $r$ after $3$ hours.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}  \n$i\\,\\,+$  \n{{field-2}}  \n$j)\\text{km}$" :question/worked-solution "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case,\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+0j,\\,u=3i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the submarine after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(-3i+0j)+(3i+5j)(3) \\\\  & =-3i+0j+9i+15j \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+15\\,j)\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47335ffc-76d6-57eb-9a83-fdf02abfce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47335ffc-76d6-57eb-9a83-fdf02abfce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306695} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c65e026-3ed0-5489-8013-e57161dd45a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9037442c-101c-5b1d-902f-85370b318b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9037442c-101c-5b1d-902f-85370b318b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9d8b0b3-2dfd-5d99-9be8-5f825f686661" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1051f019-d3c2-55aa-8b3d-d7e882c05820" :question/math-academy-id "q-280504" :question/problem "A particle moves from the origin with an initial velocity of $(6i+8j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and experiences a constant acceleration of $(-2i-10j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the ball after $1$ second.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i+8j,\\,a=-2i-10j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=1\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(6i+8j)(1)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i-10j) \\\\  & =(6i+8j)+(-1i-5j) \\\\  & =(\\,5\\,i+3\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e11a6f89-e45d-55f2-9cf5-3a573e61c6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306700} {:answer/id #uuid "0ebd4de9-ed98-5cb7-a34a-9e305896dd0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e11a6f89-e45d-55f2-9cf5-3a573e61c6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306700} :answer-field/id #uuid "659d0a08-fdac-53a0-9dce-6b38aa942d2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "446e3c86-62fe-567c-9736-ff7fb09fbe10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "446e3c86-62fe-567c-9736-ff7fb09fbe10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306703} :answer-field/id #uuid "315ad1a6-46bd-5233-af8e-3644e8d1fe8f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea3a2584-019c-5965-92b5-cae1e20c4ed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-280507" :question/problem "A toy rocket is launched from the origin with an initial velocity of $(2i+6j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(i+5j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector of the rocket after $2$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=2i+6j,\\,a=i+5j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the rocket after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(2i+6j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+5j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+2(i+5j) \\\\  & =(4i+12j)+(2i+10j) \\\\  & =(\\,6\\,i+22\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "da1d8490-fd41-5363-97d2-91b360f10723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Position Vector of a Particle Moving With Constant Acceleration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed489786-a9d6-5b3b-a37f-4960a65a28df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed489786-a9d6-5b3b-a37f-4960a65a28df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306706} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d293f1-b48a-55b5-8856-9340230cd701" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306705} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba8183b-7f3c-5c3d-a751-a97264f7f1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba8183b-7f3c-5c3d-a751-a97264f7f1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306708} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf4ce3f-3785-573b-a60e-6ea11292114a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2950a2c3-a838-583b-ab8b-2ea8945603d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280513" :question/problem "A skier begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(-3i+2j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(5i-2j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and accelerates at $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $2$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=-3i+2j,\\,u=5i-2j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(5i-2j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(8i+4j) \\\\  & =(-3i+2j)+(10i-4j)+(4i+2j) \\\\  & =(\\,11\\,i+0\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12911a5a-e222-56dc-b1f7-1b1e980b6901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12911a5a-e222-56dc-b1f7-1b1e980b6901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306711} :answer-field/id #uuid "0677a7e7-8aaf-51da-832a-2aa3fbf65e47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f61b77d9-5a00-5a3c-a675-ee9a1e23e376" :question/math-academy-id "q-280526" :question/problem "A mail truck departs from the post office at the origin and drives with a constant velocity of $(4i-3j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the truck to the origin after $2$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i-3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the truck after $t=2\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(4i-3j)(2) \\\\  & =(8i-6j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the truck to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|8i-6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8665a0d8-1aa1-5748-a7f9-5735334bc012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306902} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ef709-80ec-5e5c-9f54-a7704bfb0dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f84ef709-80ec-5e5c-9f54-a7704bfb0dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306903} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c48f7c3-575c-5400-b00a-eaa29762f740" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f056a195-eb0d-534f-b5c8-1e1d2056a427" :question/math-academy-id "q-280531" :question/problem "A car accelerates from the origin with an acceleration of $(3i-4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the car to the origin$(|r|)$ after $4$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "With constant acceleration, the position is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\mathbf r_0+\\mathbf u t+\\tfrac12\\mathbf a t^2.\n$$\n\nHere $\\mathbf r_0=\\mathbf0$, $\\mathbf u=2\\mathbf i\\,\\mathrm{m/s}$, and $\\mathbf a=(3\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j)\\,\\mathrm{m/s^2}$. At $t=4\\,\\mathrm{s}$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r(4)&=\\mathbf0+(2\\mathbf i)(4)+\\tfrac12(3\\mathbf i-4\\mathbf j)(4^2)\\\\\n&=8\\mathbf i+24\\mathbf i-32\\mathbf j\\\\\n&=(32\\mathbf i-32\\mathbf j)\\,\\mathrm m.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance to the origin is therefore\n\n$$\n|\\mathbf r(4)|=\\sqrt{32^2+(-32)^2}=\\sqrt{2048}=\\boxed{32\\sqrt2\\,\\mathrm m}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd641dd4-97a3-5c4b-bde4-de798a18e5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd641dd4-97a3-5c4b-bde4-de798a18e5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306718} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fa755fc-69d3-5109-bb16-c586e912820a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fd7864c9-0a89-5e68-91c2-2e2a463a3294" :question/math-academy-id "q-280535" :question/problem "A cyclist begins at the position $(2i-j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the cyclist to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the cyclist after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i+2j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+2(i+2j) \\\\  & =(2i-j)+(6i+2j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(10i+5j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the cyclist to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
